// The truth of the reserve set for Friedrich Wilhelm Kücken, 4 Lieder Op.47 No.3, Die stille Wasserrose (low voice):
// written from the Fr. Kistner print (Leipzig 1849, plate 1711, IMSLP #574387, data/fair/kuecken47-3/kistner), bar by
// bar. A RESERVE set (data/fair/kuecken47-3/RESERVE.md): never read by this reader, the truth checked against Audiveris
// and homr only. Heads named against their own staff lines and ledger lines (zoomed); this print draws the first ledger
// line above a staff high, and heads on ledger lines sit high on them. The voice's staff is not printed in the first
// two systems (removeEmpty all; it also hides the voice's staff on page 3's last system, where the print keeps it with
// rests -- removeEmpty cannot choose systems). Dynamics, pedalling, slurs and most articulations are not written.
// All 84 bars written (2026-11-18), then checked against Audiveris and homr bar by bar on the print (bar boxes from the
// print alone, tools/fair-truth/barboxes.py): 23 places put right, most of them chords read a step off near ledger lines
// or a head too many; four spots of reading are with the owner (docs/truth-review/kuecken47-3.md). Bar 66's left hand prints two beamed groups of 64ths and then strokes ("||||") that
// repeat the group; the repeats are written as a two-note tremolo of the same length (same sound, no unprinted heads).
// Bar 70's two-note tremolos start from a chord that holds the right-hand note too (both hands), written as printed.
title "Die stille Wasserrose"
composer "Fr. Kücken Op.47 No 3."
tempo "Andante non troppo."
octave absolute
paper { breaksOnly }
time 6/8
key d major

part voice_ { clef treble }
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }

